WEBVTT

00:00:00.657 --> 00:00:01.402
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 1

00:00:02.478 --> 00:00:06.465
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> …be wary of anyone offering you solid gold pieces of <b>advice</b>.

00:00:08.238 --> 00:00:08.962
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 2

00:00:09.822 --> 00:00:12.613
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> …middle-school pupils were much more enthusiastic

00:00:12.638 --> 00:00:16.366
about doing their homework after <b>dispensing</b> <b>advice</b> on the topic…

00:00:18.212 --> 00:00:19.010
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 3

00:00:19.853 --> 00:00:22.365
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> …than after <b>receiving</b> <b>advice</b> from teachers.

00:00:24.166 --> 00:00:24.918
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 4

00:00:25.799 --> 00:00:29.894
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> …when you consider how flattering it feels to be invited to <b>give</b> <b>advice</b>.

00:00:31.828 --> 00:00:32.617
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 5

00:00:33.487 --> 00:00:37.989
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> …we tend to assume we need to <b>seek</b> <b>advice</b> in order to obtain more knowledge…

00:00:39.778 --> 00:00:40.691
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 6

00:00:41.644 --> 00:00:45.409
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> …there are few bigger compliments you can pay another person than to <b>ask</b>,

00:00:45.437 --> 00:00:48.322
preferably sincerely, <b>for</b> their <b>advice</b>.